+<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1100" height="620" viewBox="0 0 1100 620" role="img" aria-labelledby="title desc">
+  <title id="title">What Actually Happens on an AQL Dispatch</title>
+  <desc id="desc">One shared HSA AQL queue showing how naive dispatch recreates kernarg and completion resources on every hot-path invocation, while persistent dispatch creates them once and reuses them. A batched16 capability and exact per-dispatch timing results appear below.</desc>
